        "date": "2026-02-18T22:35:47Z"
      },
      "message": "Correct and complete asserts in _Bits::extract\n\nWhen extracting a contiguous string of bits from a `_Bits` object of N bits,\nwe need to ensure 4 conditions for the (presumably unsigned) start and end\nbit positions (also presuming bit indexes are numbered in decreasing order\n(N-1)..0):\n1. start >= end    # negative range\n2. end < N         # end out of range\n3. start < N       # start out of range\n4. start - end < N # range is too large\n\nThe asserts in _Bits::extract are currently:\n- start >= end\n- end <= N\n\nOf note:\n- The second is an incorrect version of (2): off by 1.\n- (3) is missing.\n- (4) can be derived from (1) and (3), so does not need to be explicitly\n  expressed.\n\nFix the incorrect condition (2) and add the missing one (3).\n\nSigned-off-by: Paul A. Clarke <paul.clarke@qti.qualcomm.com>",
